e but  you have to do it in a safe place you  don't do it in the middle of a fight Oh  John I'm so mad at you you spent this  now let's have our money conversation  you want to pick a good time in a place  you want to have some ground rules no  judgments right we're gonna try to just  calm down we're gonna say here's what I  have maybe you have a little secret  account you've been hiding maybe you've  got some debt you've been racking up  check-in with each other about your  financial priorities maybe one of you  wants to send your kids to college and  pay the whole thing the other one might  say I don't want to do that I want  try to retire by the time I'm 64 you've  got to have these conversations you've  got to have openness and you're  absolutely right though if there are  problems bringing in an unbiased third  party a financial adviser a CPA is a  great idea secret accounts never sound  like a good idea in a marriage I'm not  opposed it comes to talking when it  comes to talking to children yeah you  know there's more and more research out  there about that it should begin very  early the discussion about finances  absolutely because money habits are  actually formed by the time you are  seven years old so you want to demystify  some of the aspects of money but that's  Amin you have to share how much you make  you want them to be comfortable with the  topic and it is absolutely imperative to  have real conversations hard  conversations with your kids as they  enter high school and say this is what  our family can do in terms of college  this is our expectation you have to do  this the other thing and you want to  guide those kids to develop good money  habits and they can talk about it not  just in the family but amongst friends  and at the workplace when it comes to  salaries in that particular this is a  really touchy issue and I think that I  was certainly raised where you don't  talk about this with your family and  your friends but having open  conversations at work can reveal pay  disparity it may help you seek a mentor  seek a manager who can guide you talk to  your friends outside of work try to  demystify this topic you may end up  making more money by having these open  comers I know a specific example of  where that happened where a younger  woman discussed it openly found out a  male was making more than her and was  able to remedy that issue by sharing  that information our conversations but  well worth yeah yeah break the taboo yes  indeed all right Jim thanks so much for  being with us
 

